<section id="top">
        <div class="page-shell about-page-intro">
            <span class="eyebrow">Quickler anywhere</span>
            <h1>Field compliance software that works in any country.</h1>
            <p class="page-lede">Quickler runs inspection and compliance workflows over WhatsApp. Because the field worker only needs the WhatsApp account already on their phone, Quickler works the same way in London, Lyon or Los Angeles. There is no national app store to clear, no local hardware to ship, and no country-specific install. The product has deep roots in UK compliance and is used by firms in the UK, Europe and the United States.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="content-duo">
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">Why it travels</p>
                        <h2>WhatsApp, photos and a PDF need no local infrastructure.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Most field software is tied to a place by its plumbing: an app store listing per region, SMS gateways per country, hardware to distribute. Quickler avoids all of that by running on infrastructure that is already global.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>WhatsApp is installed on over two billion phones across almost every country</li>
                        <li>Field workers use the account they already have, with nothing new to download</li>
                        <li>Photos and voice notes work identically on any network</li>
                        <li>The output is a PDF and a dashboard record, which mean the same thing everywhere</li>
                        <li>Data is held on EU servers, a neutral and privacy-respecting base for any region</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The result is a field compliance tool that a firm in the United States or mainland Europe can adopt in exactly the same week, and the same way, as a firm in the UK.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">Any form, any country</p>
                        <h2>UK certificates were the starting point, not the ceiling.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Quickler was first built around UK compliance work — EICR electrical reports, CP12 gas safety certificates, van walkround checks — because that is where it started. But the engine underneath is form-agnostic.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Upload your own inspection or safety form, in any country</li>
                        <li>Quickler turns it into a guided WhatsApp workflow automatically</li>
                        <li>US site safety walks, fleet and equipment checks, European field records all run the same way</li>
                        <li>Condition ratings, defect logging, photos and sign-off carry across borders unchanged</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>If your team inspects something and writes it down, Quickler can run it — wherever in the world the inspection happens.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">Track record</p>
                <h2>Built by people who have shipped field and data software internationally.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-3">
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">United Kingdom</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Where Quickler is rooted</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Quickler's first customers are UK trades and inspection firms running EICR, gas, van and site safety workflows. The UK is where the product was proven against real regulatory work.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">United States</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">International delivery in the team's DNA</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Quickler's founder has previously built and delivered field and data software for US customers in a prior venture. That international experience is why the product was designed to be country-agnostic from day one.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <span class="card-link-kicker">Europe</span>
                <h3 class="card-link-title">An EU-hosted base</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">With data hosted in Germany and a GDPR-aligned design, Quickler is a natural fit for field compliance work across the European Union.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="section-header section-header-centered">
            <div>
                <p class="section-label">Common questions</p>
                <h2>Using Quickler outside the UK.</h2>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="balanced-grid-3">
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Does it work in the US?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Yes. WhatsApp is widely used in the US and Quickler runs over it exactly as it does in the UK. Upload your inspection or safety form and Quickler builds the workflow.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Does it work in Europe?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">Yes. Data is hosted in the EU and the product is GDPR-aligned, which suits firms across the European Union.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-link">
                <h3 class="card-link-title">Do I have to use UK certificate types?</h3>
                <p class="card-link-copy">No. EICR and CP12 are just examples. You can upload any form from any country and run it as a WhatsApp workflow.</p>
            </article>
